ege Pvt. Ltd.\n• Chairman, NAMI International School Pvt. Ltd.\n• Chairman, Simrik Air Pvt. Ltd.\n• Chairman, Hydro Village Pvt. Ltd.\n• Chairman, Jurimba Hydropower Company Pvt. Ltd.\n\nIndustry Leadership Roles:\n• Past President, Airlines Operators Association of Nepal\n• President, Helicopter Society of Nepal\n\nProfessional Credentials:\n• Airline Transport Pilot License (Helicopter) – ATPL(H), License No. 015\n• Commercial Pilot License – USSR\n• Airline Transport Pilot License – United States\n• Instructor Pilot Certification – United States\n\nAircraft Experience:\nCommand and instructional experience across Bell 407GXP, AS 350 B3, BK 117 B2, MI-17 series, MI-8 series, MI-2, Bell 47, and Cessna 152 aircraft platforms.\n\nNational Honors and Decorations:\nCapt. Thapa has received several national decorations and recognitions from the Government of Nepal and national security institutions in acknowledgement of his distinguished service, aviation leadership, disaster response contributions, and commitment to national development:\n• Prabal Gorkha Dakshin Bahu, Fourth Class (2003)\n• Prakhyat Trishakti Patta, Fourth Class (2005)\n• Sukirtimaya Rastradeep (2021)\n• Rastrasewa Padak (2002)\n• Nepal Police Medal (2002)\n• Daivik Prakop Padak (2001)\n• Public Service Award, Fourth Class (2011)\n• Bravery Awards from Nepal Police (2010 and 2013)\n\nOther Professional Recognitions:\n• National Personality Award (2003)\n• Best Pilot of the Year (2003)\n• Man of the Year (2004)\n\nLegacy, Vision and Leadership Philosophy:\nCapt. Thapa’s career represents a distinctive combination of aviation excellence, entrepreneurial vision, and institution-building leadership. His contributions across diverse sectors reflect his commitment to creating sustainable enterprises that generate economic value while supporting Nepal’s broader development goals. Through Annapurna Ventures and its affiliated institutions, he continues to promote innovation, responsible governance, and sustainable growth.",
